       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. At that dose there's a serious risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac toxicity (QT prolongation). It may be a typo, for example 100 mg instead of 1000 mg.\n\nAlso, medication orders normally need to come from a licensed prescriber. If you're relaying this for a clinician, please have the prescriber confirm the intended dose or enter the order themselves.\n\nIf the intended dose is within the usual range, send it and I'll enter it right away. Typical adult dosing is 25\u201350 mg once daily to start, titrated up to 200 mg/day. If the 1000 mg dose is truly intended, I'd need explicit confirmation from the prescriber, and pharmacy review would be advisable."
